---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
const title='Understanding Your Cash Offer: What You Avoid With an As-Is Sale';
const description='Received a CashAsIs offer? See the repairs, cleanup, showings, commissions, traditional buyer inspection negotiations, financing delays, and holding costs you can avoid with a direct as-is sale.';
const pubDate=new Date('2026-09-22');
const faq=[
 {q:'Is a cash offer the same as a traditional financed offer?',a:'Not necessarily. The price is only one part of an offer. Compare the purchase terms, property-condition requirements, financing, closing timeline, costs, contingencies, and work expected from you.'},
 {q:'Do I have to make repairs before selling to CashAsIs?',a:'CashAsIs purchases properties as-is, so sellers are not expected to renovate or make the property retail-ready before selling.'},
 {q:'Should I compare a cash offer directly with a possible list price?',a:'A possible list price and an actual purchase offer are different things. When comparing options, consider the potential sale price together with commissions or compensation, closing costs, repairs, concessions, holding costs, financing risk, and time.'},
 {q:'Does receiving a CashAsIs offer obligate me to sell?',a:'No. Review the proposed terms and ask questions. A seller should understand the agreement before deciding whether to sign.'},
 {q:'Does CashAsIs buy land too?',a:'Yes. CashAsIs works with houses and land, and each property and offer is evaluated individually.'}
];
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head>
<BaseHead title={title} description={description} type="article" pubDate={pubDate} author="CashAsIs" faq={faq}/>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css"/>
<style>.offer-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:12px;margin:22px 0}.offer-item{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:18px;background:#fbfcfd}.offer-item b{display:block;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:5px}.offer-item span{font-size:14px;color:#566273;line-height:1.5}@media(max-width:640px){.offer-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
</head><body>
<Nav/>
<section class="legal-hero"><div class="in"><span class="badge">Cash Offer Guide</span><h1>Your CashAsIs Offer Is More Than a Number</h1><p class="meta">See the costs, work, showings, negotiations, and delays you are avoiding with a direct as-is sale.</p></div></section>
<main class="legal-wrap"><article class="legal-card article">
<p class="eyebrow"><a href="/blog/">&larr; More Seller Resources</a></p>
<div class="article-body">
<p><strong>Your CashAsIs offer is the purchase price we're offering for your property under the terms of the agreement.</strong> The items below are not extra deductions from our offer. They are examples of costs, work, and traditional-sale steps you are avoiding by selling directly to CashAsIs as-is.</p>
<div class="callout"><p><b>KNOW WHAT YOU'RE SAVING — NOT JUST WHAT YOU'RE SELLING FOR.</b><br/>No repairs before selling &bull; No cleanup or staging &bull; No traditional showings &bull; No Realtor commission charged by CashAsIs &bull; No waiting on buyer mortgage approval</p></div>
<h2>Your offer is not a starting point for a list of repair deductions</h2>
<p>When CashAsIs makes an as-is offer, we are evaluating the property in its current condition. You are not being asked to renovate the kitchen, replace flooring, repaint, stage the property, or make it retail-ready before selling to us. The purpose of an as-is offer is to give you a clear path to sell without first taking on that work.</p>
<div class="offer-grid">
<div class="offer-item"><b>REPAIRS</b><span>Avoid spending money fixing or renovating the property before the sale.</span></div>
<div class="offer-item"><b>CLEANUP &amp; PREP</b><span>Avoid the traditional process of getting the property cleaned, staged, photographed, and show-ready.</span></div>
<div class="offer-item"><b>SHOWINGS</b><span>Avoid repeated buyer appointments, open houses, and keeping the property ready for visitors.</span></div>
<div class="offer-item"><b>BUYER FINANCING</b><span>Avoid waiting on a traditional buyer's mortgage underwriting, lender approval, and financing process.</span></div>
</div>
<h2>Avoid traditional buyer inspection and repair negotiations</h2>
<p>In a traditional sale, a buyer may conduct inspections and then request repairs, credits, concessions, or a price adjustment depending on the contract. With CashAsIs, the property is being purchased as-is, so you are avoiding that traditional post-inspection repair-negotiation process.</p>
<p><strong>As-is does not mean known property issues should be hidden.</strong> Any disclosure obligations or representations required by your transaction still apply. The difference is that you are not preparing the property for a retail buyer and then negotiating a new repair list after a traditional buyer inspection.</p>
<h2>Avoid Realtor commission charged by CashAsIs</h2>
<p>CashAsIs is buying directly rather than listing your property for you, so CashAsIs does not charge you a listing-agent commission for the purchase. If you have a separate agreement with a real estate broker, agent, or another party, review that agreement because it may create obligations independent of CashAsIs.</p>
<h2>Avoid waiting on a buyer's mortgage</h2>
<p>A traditional financed buyer may need underwriting, lender approval, an appraisal, and other financing requirements. CashAsIs is presenting a cash offer, so the purchase is not dependent on that traditional buyer mortgage-approval process. Title work and the terms of your purchase agreement still apply.</p>
<h2>Time can cost money too</h2>
<p>While you continue owning a property, expenses such as taxes, insurance, utilities, mortgage interest, HOA charges, lawn care, security, and maintenance can continue where applicable. A direct sale can reduce the amount of time you spend preparing and marketing a property, although the actual closing timeline depends on your agreement and title requirements.</p>
<h2>So what should you compare?</h2>
<p>If you are deciding between your CashAsIs offer and another way of selling, don't compare our actual offer only to a hoped-for list price. Compare what you may actually receive after the expenses and requirements of each option, along with the time and work each route requires.</p>
<div class="callout"><p><b>YOUR CASHASIS OFFER:</b><br/>A direct as-is purchase price + fewer traditional selling steps to deal with.<br/><br/><b>A TRADITIONAL SALE MAY ALSO INVOLVE:</b><br/>Repairs &bull; Preparation &bull; Showings &bull; Negotiated commissions/compensation &bull; Inspections &bull; Buyer financing &bull; Concessions &bull; Continued holding costs</p></div>
<h2>Have questions about your specific offer?</h2>
<p>Ask your CashAsIs representative about any term you do not understand before deciding. You can also read <a href="/why-sell-as-is/">what selling as-is means</a>, see our <a href="/no-repairs-no-cleanup/">no repairs or cleanup guide</a>, or browse the <a href="/seller-faq/">Seller FAQ</a>.</p>
</div>
<section class="faq"><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>{faq.map((f)=><details><summary>{f.q}</summary><p>{f.a}</p></details>)}</section>
</article></main><Footer/>
<script is:inline src="https://link.msgsndr.com/js/external-tracking.js" data-tracking-id="tk_61336d42285a45a29bdc44b9a0947ddf"></script>
</body></html>